  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 326 AM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nOver the weekend into early next week, global model guidance is in \nagreement that quasi-zonal to slightly southwesterly upper-level \nflow will prevail over the Mid-Mississippi River Valley with a \nseries of upper-level troughs grazing the region. This pattern will \ncause a front to waver between the Mid-Mississippi River Valley and \nMidwest that is reflected by an extended period of varying PoPs \nacross the CWA. Ensemble model membership with measurable rainfall \nis highest Friday night into Saturday and again Monday night into \nTuesday, but there is no single member that has precipitation during \nthis entire period. So, although there will be opportunities for \nshowers and thunderstorms, much of this time will be dry vs. wet. \nWith the CWA residing near or south of the front through this period \nas well, above average high temperatures will vary mainly from the \nmid-80s to low-90s F. The NBM interquartile range quickly inflates \nto 15 F next Tuesday onward, spread from similar above average \ntemperatures to temperatures closer to average if the front shifts \nsouth of the CWA.",
